## Why This Is Asked

Assess ability to design a compliant, scalable OpenAI integration with policy guardrails in a multi-tenant fintech context, including data lineage and auditability.

## Key Concepts

- Guardrails and policy engine for PII and regulatory compliance
- Per-tenant RBAC via Azure AD and Purview metadata
- Grounding OpenAI outputs to a versioned KB in Blob via Cognitive Search
- Auditing and data lake lineage, retention, and tamper resistance
- Validation plan with synthetic prompts, redaction checks, and leakage tests

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo-code: illustrate policy check flow
function checkPolicy(tenantId, prompt) {
  const policies = loadPolicies(tenantId);
  if (containsPII(prompt) || violatesRegulations(prompt, policies)) {
    redact(prompt);
    throw new Error("Policy violation");
  }
  return prompt;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you test for prompt injection across tenants in this setup?
- How would you scale the policy engine to support 100s of tenants with individualized rules?

## Why This Is Asked

